 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`theorem endZeroAlgEquiv_of_linearize_map (f : (TLDiagCat.of 0 : TLDiagCat) \u27f6 .of 0) : endZeroAlgEquiv (End.of ((linearize R \u03b4).map f)) = \u03b4 ^ f.diagram.circles` is stated with no attribute. The neighbouring evaluation lemmas `endZeroAlgEquiv_apply` and `endZeroAlgEquiv_symm_apply` are `@[simp]`. `linearize_map` is not `@[simp]`, so simp cannot reach this value through the other lemmas.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/TemperleyLieb/Category.lean",
   "fix": "Rename it to `endZeroAlgEquiv_linearize_map` and tag it `@[simp]`.",
   "issue": "`endZeroAlgEquiv_of_linearize_map` is the evaluation lemma for `endZeroAlgEquiv` on images of `linearize`. Its `_of_` infix reads as a hypothesis, and it has no `@[simp]`, so `endZeroAlgEquiv (End.of ((linearize R \u03b4).map f))` does not reduce automatically to `\u03b4 ^ f.diagram.circles`.",
   "line": 0
  }
